    "findings": [
      "Serprog v1 SPI-only requires O_SPIOP and capability negotiation; parallel opbuf is not needed.",
      "CS spans complete write and read phases; no TCP waits while CS is low.",
      "Raw transactions cannot determine generic internal busy state. YAML confirms target readiness and memory idle; no opcode database or guessed erase deadline.",
      "The Flash driver needs a software session reservation in addition to its verified GPIO/CFG lease.",
      "Independent nested addrspi caches are unsafe on shared address wires; address levels must be reapplied for each frame.",
      "SPI delegates have no transfer error return; memory protocol/data verification stays with flashrom and cleanup policy."
    ]
  },
